      "sc:author": "Fishka Bio",
      "sc:citation": {
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21444547"
      },
      "sc:description": "Browser-based tool to open almost any file that carries sequence — FASTA, FASTQ, GenBank, EMBL, Swiss-Prot, AB1/ABIF, SCF, Clustal, Stockholm, PHYLIP, NEXUS, MSF, PIR, MEGA, GFF3, SAM, BAM, GFA, PDB and ACE — see every sequence inside, pick the ones you want, and save them as FASTA. The format is detected from the file content, not from the extension, so unlabelled or misnamed files still open, and gzip-compressed files are unpacked in place. Turns any of them into FASTA without a command line and without an account. Runs entirely in the browser — files are never uploaded.",
      "sc:featureList": [
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_0233"
        },
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_2121"
        }
      ],
